   "content": "**Women are at least half of researchers in 23 of the 104 countries with recent data.** The highest shares:\n\n- **Myanmar:** 76.5% (2023)\n- **Kyrgyzstan:** 61.4% (2024)\n- **Azerbaijan:** 60.6% (2024)\n- **Albania:** 57.7% (2022)\n- **Mongolia:** 57.4% (2022)\n\nIn the typical country, 43% of researchers are women. The map shades countries above parity (50%) and below it in different colours. It uses each country's latest headcount from 2019–2024. Source: UIS, February 2026 release; indicator FRESP.THC.",
